    "start": 75.22,
    "end": 102.64,
    "text": "Georgie, you've been looking at the research on this. Do scientists think that what we eat affects how we sleep? Yes, they do. Scientists have done some long -term studies, so looking at large groups of people over a long period of time. And they found that a healthier diet is associated with better quality sleep. They've also done some smaller studies, looking in more detail at exactly what people are eating, and then studying how they sleep in a laboratory.",
